Negative control for form-cutover.test.ts — the reference-data seam.

Drops the wrapper's `provideFormEngineData({ countries, ensureCountries })` call,
so the engine's phone control gets no country list from the host: the country
picker opens empty and nothing ever asks the host to load the list. The icon
seam, the host binding and the model round-trip are untouched.

The now-unused `useSystem` destructure and import go with it. Left behind they
trip `noUnusedLocals` and the mutant grades TYPECHECK instead of the assertion.

Expected: the two assertions under "the wrapper's country list reaches the phone
control" that read the wrapper path go red — "offers the countries the host
supplied, and nothing else" and "asks the host to load the list". The paired
bare-engine control, "offers no country on a host nobody supplied a list to",
must stay GREEN; that pairing is what separates a real seam assertion from one
passing on ambient state. Both icon assertions stay green.

